# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout.
# For a repository driven entirely by shell scripts that is fatal and invisible: bash reads the
# trailing \r as part of the command and every script dies with
#
#     $'\r': command not found
#
# which says nothing about line endings. The `eol=lf` entries below override autocrlf per file
# type, so a Windows clone gets working scripts regardless of the user's global Git settings.

* text=auto

# Anything with a shebang, or read by an interpreter, must keep LF.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# Git hooks are shell scripts without an extension.
.githooks/*  text eol=lf

# Source and config: LF everywhere, so a Windows contributor's diffs stay readable to everyone.
*.cs       text eol=lf
*.csproj   text eol=lf
*.props    text eol=lf
*.xml      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.toml     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf

# Binary, so Git never tries to translate them. The mesh atlas especially: a CRLF rewrite would
# corrupt it silently and the failure would show up as garbage geometry in game, not as an error.
*.glb   binary
*.png   binary
*.ktx2  binary
*.zip   binary
*.dll   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.exe   binary

# Generated and not worth diffing in a review.
docs/KSA-API-SURFACE.md  linguist-generated=true
CHANGELOG.md             linguist-generated=true
